title: Web (WASM) Client
description: Browser-side unpack/pack UI.
---

# Web Client

The Artemis web client provides a graphical interface for packing and unpacking archives directly in your browser. It's built with TypeScript, SolidJS, and Tailwind CSS, and uses WebAssembly (WASM) for high-performance archive processing.

## Build the WASM Payload

First, compile the Go code into WebAssembly:

```bash
GOOS=js GOARCH=wasm go build -o web/public/artemis.wasm ./cmd/wasm
cp "$(go env GOROOT)/lib/wasm/wasm_exec.js" web/public/
```

## Run the Frontend

Next, install dependencies and run the Vite development server:

```bash
cd web
npm install
npm run dev
```
